{%- comment -%}
  Answers one question: will onrepeat-buy-module actually render for this product?

  Outputs "1" when it will and nothing at all when it will not, so a caller can
  capture the render and test the captured string against blank.

  WHY IT IS ITS OWN SNIPPET
  Two places need the answer and they must never disagree:

    1. onrepeat-buy-module.liquid, deciding whether to render itself.
    2. main-product.liquid, deciding whether to draw the shipping/trust strip
       above the variant picker — the module carries its own copy of that strip
       under the buttons, and two identical gold hairline strips 150px apart is
       worse than either one alone.

  If the condition were written twice, a product could lose both strips (the
  section suppresses, the module declines) or gain two. Keeping it here means
  that cannot happen.

  Accepts:
  - product {Object} required
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign bma_size_index = nil
  for opt in product.options_with_values
    assign opt_down = opt.name | downcase
    if opt_down contains 'size'
      assign bma_size_index = forloop.index0
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}
{%- if bma_size_index != nil and product.options_with_values.size == 1 and product.variants.size > 0 -%}1{%- endif -%}
